# Semantic, logical git commits

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). **Always** use Conventional Commits. Never write unstructured subjects.

Format: `<type>(optional-scope): <imperative summary>`

When committing, **always split work into logical commits** (one concern each):

- Do not dump an entire session or mixed features into one catch-all commit
- Keep tests and docs that belong to that concern in the same commit
- Do not mix a feature with an unrelated cleanup, rename, or formatting pass
- Stage whole files by path (`git add path`). Do not use `git add -p` or `git add -i`
- If one file mixes concerns, still commit the other files separately
- Do not commit `dist/`, `.plugin-build-cache/`, or `script/docker/dev/.image-built`
